{"hash":"4e04fb427437e631","voice":"en-IN-NeerjaExpressiveNeural","rate":"+4%","dur":64.75,"said":"Step through this low doorway and let your eyes settle on the silver. Remember the shikhara you looked up at, three shrines stacked on one line? You are standing in the middle one. Far beneath your feet, below the earth, sits Mahakal, the lord of time, facing south. Here, on the earth, sits Shri Omkareshwar Mahadev. The name belongs to another Jyotirlinga too, on an island in the Narmada about a hundred and forty kilometres south of Ujjain, and many pilgrims feel that bowing here honours both. Watch the people around you. Most have just come up from darshan below, and on their way out they stop here for a moment, touch the step, and fold their hands. Some say the three shrines are one prayer offered in three places: the Lord beneath the earth, the Lord upon it, and the Lord above it. The third is over your head right now, on the top storey, behind a door that is almost always shut. Go back out into the hall, and look for the stair on its west side.","segments":[{"key":"text","start":0,"end":962}],"words":[[0.098,0.349,0,4],[0.459,0.192,5,12],[0.663,0.24,13,17],[0.915,0.18,18,21],[1.108,0.541,22,29],[1.661,0.228,30,33],[1.901,0.24,34,37],[2.153,0.132,38,42],[2.298,0.192,43,47],[2.502,0.349,48,54],[2.862,0.132,55,57],[3.007,0.084,58,61],[3.103,0.481,62,68],[4.423,0.493,70,78],[4.928,0.096,79,82],[5.036,0.433,83,91],[5.481,0.108,92,95],[5.601,0.264,96,102],[5.877,0.216,103,105],[6.106,0.264,106,108],[6.538,0.252,110,115],[6.803,0.445,116,123],[7.26,0.385,124,131],[7.656,0.18,132,134],[7.849,0.216,135,138],[8.077,0.373,139,143],[9.303,0.204,145,148],[9.519,0.108,149,152],[9.639,0.481,153,161],[10.132,0.084,162,164],[10.228,0.072,165,168],[10.312,0.337,169,175],[10.661,0.385,176,179],[11.923,0.337,181,184],[12.272,0.337,185,192],[12.62,0.156,193,197],[12.788,0.445,198,202],[13.486,0.288,204,209],[13.786,0.144,210,213],[13.942,0.288,214,219],[14.435,0.312,221,225],[14.76,0.6